Subject: [M156] [compiler] Mark string-keyed ordered hash lookups as writing

Original change's description:
> [compiler] Mark string-keyed ordered hash lookups as writing
>
> FindOrderedHashMapEntry and FindOrderedHashSetEntry can internalize a
> non-internalized string key in place into a ThinString via
> String::MakeThin (since https://crrev.com/c/6965654), overwriting its
> payload (e.g., ConsString::first_ with ThinString::actual_).
>
> Declare heap write effects on string-keyed ordered hash table lookups in
> Turboshaft, TurboFan, and Maglev so load elimination, value numbering,
> and dead-code elimination do not reuse stale string fields across them,
> while keeping Int32 Map lookups read-only and non-allocating.
>
